{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nSix surviving Python modules under `tests/unit/plan_review` contain 8 audited, verbose leading docstrings. The historical audit was at `origin/main@9e6a0e436520f67962c22dc244d7b4f77f5bee45`; executable scope and before citations are refreshed to `origin/main@a74d0073e84fc8b772f79b6ed1b1af13d0df67c6`. The deleted `test_det_floor_module_seam.py` and its 2 blocks are retired from this leaf; the stable IDs below replace mutable line ranges. The old ranges also selected five short, load-bearing comment blocks that already state current constraints concisely; those false positives are protected rather than edited.\n\n## Approach\nEdit only the stable-ID blocks below. Capture current-parent (`a74d0073e84fc8b772f79b6ed1b1af13d0df67c6`) before/final blobs for every owned path and parse both with `ast.parse(..., type_comments=True)`. On comparison copies, remove only an allowlisted leading `Expr(Constant(str))` that is the first statement of a `Module`, `ClassDef`, `FunctionDef`, or `AsyncFunctionDef`; normalize only `ast.TypeIgnore.lineno`; require the remaining normalized ASTs to match.\n\nTokenize both blobs and reject every changed inline comment or non-allowlisted full-line comment. Preserve non-docstring runtime strings, regexes, prompts, imports, decorators, annotations, assertions, subprocess arguments, test data, shebangs, and complete directive-bearing physical lines exactly. Adjacent blank-line normalization is allowed only around an edited block.\n\n## Stable block allowlist\n- `tests/unit/plan_review/test_2be7_whitespace_material.py` — 3 blocks:\n  - `D:<module>`\n  - `D:test_whitespace_only_edit_leaves_attestation_certified`\n  - `D:test_legacy_algorithm_still_hashes_the_raw_description`\n- `tests/unit/plan_review/test_94a3_material_diff.py`:\n  - `D:<module>`\n- `tests/unit/plan_review/test_criteria_blocking.py`:\n  - `D:<module>`\n- `tests/unit/plan_review/test_det_criterion_gates.py`:\n  - `D:<module>`\n- `tests/unit/plan_review/test_g7_blocking.py`:\n  - `D:<module>`\n- `tests/unit/plan_review/test_t5c_grounding.py`:\n  - `D:<module>`\n\n`D:<symbol>` means the true leading docstring owned by that module/function. No other prose is editable.\n\n## Protected false positives\nKeep exact the current full-line blocks before `d = _decided(\"omits_required_site\")` in `test_g7_blocking.py` and before `text = _text()` in `test_t5c_grounding.py`. They record non-obvious ownership, binding, grading, and cross-rubric constraints in 2–3 lines each.\n\n## Preserved contracts and consumers\n- Whitespace-only material edits remain certified; meaningful indentation/content edits stale; legacy raw-description fingerprints remain byte-compatible.\n- Component-specific staleness diagnostics, checkbox normalization, legacy handling, and gate outcomes remain unchanged.\n- T3/T10/T5c/G7 posture thresholds, deterministic trigger/skip evidence, grading, grounding, deduplication, and severity scoping remain intact.\n- The owned modules are direct pytest inputs. `test_threshold_recalibration.py`, `test_plan_review_g7.py`, and `test_module_size_contract.py` remain focused companion/helper consumers. No target module import, `__doc__`, `inspect.getdoc`, or pydoc consumer was found.\n\nPreserve this complete directive-bearing physical line byte-for-byte:\n\n```python\n    from rebar.llm.workflow import steps as _steps  # noqa: F401 — registers the ops\n```\n\nAll other inline comments also remain unchanged.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] Only declared stable-ID blocks and adjacent blank lines change; normalized-AST and token/comment comparisons pass on every owned path.\n- [x] Every edited block is shorter and retains its listed current contract while removing chronology, duplication, obvious narration, or separator ornament.\n- [x] An independent reviewer posts one leaf-linked TSV row per block: `stable_block_id<TAB>before_citation<TAB>final_citation<TAB>preserved_contract_or_consumer<TAB>directives_exact<TAB>before_words<TAB>after_words<TAB>semantic-preservation<TAB>bloat-removal<TAB>reviewer_session`.\n- [x] Every expected row has current-parent before citations and `directives_exact=PASS`, `semantic-preservation=PASS`, and `bloat-removal=PASS`; missing/failing rows block closure.\n- [x] All five structured verify commands pass.\n\n## Verification\nThe five DD-level commands recorded on this ticket run focused pytest (including named consumers), scoped Ruff check plus format-check, comment hygiene, owned-path `git diff --check`, and worktree-venv `make verify`. They are the executable completion oracle.\n\n\n## Merged completion evidence\nGerrit 3088 merged `f53902d840d04b37f3ef059bc9e7ad6d3885f963` from signed candidate `2270033517515ba1686418741b607db437622af7` (candidate parent `a74d0073e84fc8b772f79b6ed1b1af13d0df67c6`; all 20 before/final path blobs preserved through server rebase). LLM-Review +1, Verified +1, zero unresolved comments; CI run 40047061920 succeeded. Untimed local `make verify`: 19,712 passed, 93 skipped, exit 0. All recorded focused, structural, directive, path, diff, hygiene, and applicable scoped Ruff commands exited 0. Nonauthor reviewer agent `/root/resume_group02` posted 8 exact merged-SHA PASS rows; Rebar Bot is the shared transport identity. The shared commit changes 20 paths; this leaf owns 6 Scope paths.\n"}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1792807325248025253,"uuid":"cefed3ba-916b-4bab-8028-40f373f5a03d"}